// Draft occupation dataset: one-time LLM-assisted trait-profile pass.
// trait_profile dimensions (0-1 each):
//   quadrant_a: analytical/quantitative (Financial Analyst archetype)
//   quadrant_b: sequential/structured (ER Physician archetype)
//   quadrant_c: relational/interpersonal (Executive/People Leader archetype)
//   quadrant_d: experimental/big-picture (Startup Founder archetype)
//   pace_preference: 0 = slow/deliberate, 1 = fast/urgent
//   risk_tolerance: 0 = risk-averse, 1 = risk-seeking
//
// `median_salary` and `growth_pct` are approximate, drawn from general
// knowledge of recent BLS/industry ranges, NOT a live pull. Kept for
// display/quadrant purposes but superseded for anything outlook-related
// by the real, sourced `bls_*` fields added 2026-07-20 (see below).
// Prefer those wherever accuracy matters.
//
// Rebalanced 2026-07-18 per founder direction: primary audience is
// ambitious high schoolers/university students aiming at high-earning,
// "logically advanced" long-term careers (finance, tech, healthcare, law,
// engineering, bioengineering, pharma, consulting). That set is deep and
// wide below. A small, clearly-secondary ALTERNATIVE PATHS section at the
// end covers skilled trades, aviation, hospitality, and similar, present
// for users who genuinely want that, but deliberately not competing for
// coverage with the main set.

//
// Dominance-sharpened 2026-07-18: every trait_profile rewritten so each
// occupation maps to ONE clearly dominant HBDI quadrant (0.85-0.98), per
// founder direction: prior pass had too many occupations with two
// closely-tied quadrant scores, which flattened cosine-similarity match
// results.
//
// Real BLS data added 2026-07-20: soc_code, bls_change_pct_2024_34,
// bls_median_wage_2024, bls_annual_openings_thousands, bls_match_confidence,
// bls_match_note. Sourced from the actual U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics
// Employment Projections, 2024-34 cycle, Table 1.2 (bls.gov/emp/tables/
// occupational-projections-and-characteristics.htm). Every SOC code and
// number was cross-checked against that source table programmatically,
// zero mismatches. Not every occupation has a clean 1:1 BLS match: see
// bls_match_confidence ('exact' | 'close' | 'approximate' | 'no_match');
// fields are null rather than guessed when no reasonable match exists.
// Advisory content (how_to_break_in, typical_progression,
// skills_to_build_first, common_misconceptions, interview_focus) is a
// first-draft LLM-assisted pass, same review process as trait_profile,
// flagged for founder review before treating as final.
